                <pb facs="0247" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg241"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Nicaragua claims sovereignty over Mosquito Reservation; placed troops; Bluefields
                    declared martial law. Mosquito authorities protested; asked protection British
                    consul. English soldiers landed later. English and Nicaraguan troops temporarily
                    withdrawn. Referred to British minister, Guatemala.</p>
            </div>
